# The number of `errcheck` findings tolerated in the tree. This is a RATCHET,
# exactly like .interface-width-baseline: CI fails if the count goes UP, and
# also fails if it goes DOWN without this number being lowered in the same PR.
#
# Why this exists. Wave 0 of the silent-failure sweep
# (docs/audits/2026-08-11-silent-failure-error-discards.md) wired errcheck into
# .golangci.yml with the bucket-(f) exclude list, but the config was never
# actually gated anywhere -- `make ci` does not run it, and
# .github/workflows/ci.yml's `golangci-lint-args: '--enable-only nolintlint'`
# deliberately leaves errcheck out, with a comment reading "When Wave 0 closes,
# add errcheck here". Wave 0 never closed the backlog to zero (waves 4-13 pay it
# down file by file), so a bare pass/fail gate on errcheck is permanently red at
# this baseline and would get switched off by whoever saw it next -- the exact
# failure mode .golangci.yml's own header warns about for the un-exempted case.
# A ratchet answers "did the count go UP", which can gate from day one, same
# shape as the interface-width ratchet solved for interfacebloat.
#
# Baseline measured 2026-09-25 with a freshly scoped golangci-lint cache
# (scripts/check-errcheck-ratchet.sh's own GOLANGCI_LINT_CACHE scoping), on
# origin/proposed-main plus Wave 0's already-landed primitives (bed1db5a2). This
# is the pre-existing backlog `make lint-errcheck` already reported red; nothing
# in this PR fixes any of it. Lower this number in the same PR as any fix that
# closes findings, exactly as the interface-width baseline instructs.
834
